flowchart TB
  accTitle: Proposed B4 intention lifecycle
  accDescr: A proposed intention is either authorized or rejected by the proposal authority. An authorized intention becomes active. A validated trigger moves it to reconsideration pending, where the governor may continue, switch method, delegate, or suspend. A delegated child returns success, failure, timeout, or cancellation to parent reconsideration after scope and version validation. A suspended intention resumes to its recorded active or reconsideration target only after conditions and permissions are revalidated. Satisfaction, impossibility, rejection, and abandonment are terminal for the relevant proposal or intention version.
  P[PROPOSED] -->|goal authority approves| A[AUTHORIZED]
  P -->|proposal authority rejects with reason| REJ[REJECTED]
  A -->|initial method passes checks| X[ACTIVE]
  X -->|validated trigger or scheduled review| R[RECONSIDERATION PENDING]
  R -->|continue| X
  R -->|switch method; preserve goal version| X
  R -->|delegate bounded child| D[DELEGATED]
  D -->|success, failure, timeout, or cancellation; parent scope and version revalidated| R
  D -->|late or unverifiable result; suspend and escalate| S
  X -->|pause with resume condition| S[SUSPENDED]
  R -->|pause with resume condition| S
  S -->|resumeTarget ACTIVE; condition and permissions revalidated| X
  S -->|resumeTarget RECONSIDERATION_PENDING; new review required| R
  X -->|verified goal success| SAT[SATISFIED]
  R -->|verified goal success| SAT
  X -->|evidence proves impossible| IMP[IMPOSSIBLE]
  R -->|evidence proves impossible| IMP
  X -->|authorized abandonment| AB[ABANDONED]
  R -->|authorized abandonment| AB
  S -->|authorized abandonment| AB
  classDef source fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef process fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef output fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef caution fill:#FEF9E7,stroke:#F39C12,color:#1C1C1E
